WEBVTT

00:00:07.684 --> 00:00:08.768
(PANTING)

00:00:11.855 --> 00:00:13.148
Who are you?

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:15.984
-I'm sorry.
-Who are you?

00:00:16.818 --> 00:00:19.362
-Newt Scamander. And you are?
-What's that thing in your case?

00:00:20.405 --> 00:00:21.531
That's my Niffler.

00:00:22.532 --> 00:00:24.367
Say, you've got something on your--

00:00:24.784 --> 00:00:27.037
Why in the name of Deliverance Dane
did you let that thing loose?

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:28.955
I didn't mean to.
He's incorrigible, you see.

00:00:29.122 --> 00:00:31.291
-Anything shiny, he's all over--
-You didn't mean to?

00:00:31.458 --> 00:00:32.542
-No.
-You could not have chosen

00:00:32.709 --> 00:00:35.170
a worse time to let that creature loose.

00:00:35.337 --> 00:00:37.339
We're in the middle of a situation here.

00:00:39.674 --> 00:00:40.675
I'm taking you in.

00:00:40.842 --> 00:00:42.385
Taking me in where?

00:00:43.428 --> 00:00:45.013
Magical Congress of
the United States of America.

00:00:48.558 --> 00:00:50.227
So you work for MACUSA.

00:00:51.686 --> 00:00:53.188
What are you, some kind of investigator?

00:00:56.024 --> 00:00:57.734
At least tell me
you took care of the No-Maj.

00:00:58.485 --> 00:01:00.153
-The what?
-The No-Maj.

00:01:01.696 --> 00:01:03.782
No-Magic. The non-wizard!

00:01:04.991 --> 00:01:06.117
Oh. Sorry, we call them Muggles.

00:01:06.284 --> 00:01:07.827
You wiped his memory, right?

00:01:08.328 --> 00:01:09.996
The No-Maj with the case?

00:01:11.998 --> 00:01:13.208
-Um...
-Oh...

00:01:14.084 --> 00:01:16.461
That's a Section 3-A, Mr. Scamander.

00:01:16.753 --> 00:01:17.837
I'm taking you in.

00:01:19.381 --> 00:01:20.924
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

00:01:26.763 --> 00:01:27.764
TINA: Come on.

00:01:29.933 --> 00:01:32.352
Sorry, but I do have
things to do, actually.

00:01:32.519 --> 00:01:35.313
Well... (SCOFFS)
You'll have to rearrange them.

00:01:36.231 --> 00:01:38.149
What are you doin' in New York anyway?

00:01:38.316 --> 00:01:39.734
I came to buy a birthday present.

00:01:40.569 --> 00:01:41.611
Couldn't you have done that in London?

00:01:42.612 --> 00:01:44.906
NEWT: No, there's only one breeder
of Appaloosa Puffskeins in the world,

00:01:45.073 --> 00:01:47.200
and he lives in New York. So, no.

00:01:48.493 --> 00:01:50.120
I got a Section 3-A.

00:01:52.122 --> 00:01:53.206
Hey.

00:01:53.373 --> 00:01:57.085
By the way, we don't allow the breeding
of magical creatures in New York.

00:01:57.252 --> 00:01:59.588
We closed that guy down a year ago.

00:02:12.851 --> 00:02:17.188
MAGICAL EXPOSURE THREAT LEVEL
SEVERE UNEXPLAINED ACTIVITY

00:02:48.428 --> 00:02:49.804
Hey, Goldstein.

00:02:50.513 --> 00:02:51.681
Hey, Red.

00:02:53.933 --> 00:02:54.934
(TINA CLEARS THROAT)

00:02:55.602 --> 00:02:56.895
Major Investigation Department.

00:02:57.062 --> 00:02:59.147
-I thought you was--
-Major Investigation Department.

00:02:59.314 --> 00:03:00.732
I got a Section 3-A.

00:03:05.737 --> 00:03:08.406
MAGICAL DISTURBANCES
RISK WIZARDING EXPOSURE

00:03:08.573 --> 00:03:11.701
The International Confederation
is threatening to send a delegation.

00:03:12.702 --> 00:03:15.580
They think this is related to
Grindelwald's attacks in Europe.

00:03:15.872 --> 00:03:17.457
I was there.

00:03:18.541 --> 00:03:19.876
This is a beast.

00:03:20.543 --> 00:03:24.339
No human could do what this thing
is capable of, Madam President.

00:03:25.256 --> 00:03:28.051
Whatever it is, one thing is clear.
It must be stopped.

00:03:28.385 --> 00:03:29.719
It's terrorizing No-Majs.

00:03:29.886 --> 00:03:32.847
And when No-Majs are afraid, they attack.

00:03:33.598 --> 00:03:35.183
This could mean exposure.

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:36.476
It could mean war.

00:03:36.726 --> 00:03:37.727
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

00:03:44.317 --> 00:03:47.362
I made your position here
quite clear, Ms. Goldstein.

00:03:47.737 --> 00:03:50.699
-Yes, Madam President. But I--
-You're no longer an Auror.

00:03:53.576 --> 00:03:56.579
No, Madam President, but--

00:03:56.746 --> 00:03:57.872
Goldstein.

00:03:58.039 --> 00:03:59.124
There's been a minor--

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:03.628
This office is currently concerned
with very major incidents. Get out.

00:04:03.795 --> 00:04:04.838
Yes, ma'am.

00:04:21.271 --> 00:04:23.106
(SQUEAKING)

00:04:24.607 --> 00:04:27.026
WAND PERMIT OFFICE

00:04:31.281 --> 00:04:32.824
So you got your wand permit?

00:04:32.991 --> 00:04:35.118
All foreigners have to
have them in New York.

00:04:35.452 --> 00:04:37.954
I made a postal application weeks ago.

00:04:42.459 --> 00:04:43.918
TINA: Scamander...

00:04:44.586 --> 00:04:46.546
And you were just in Equatorial Guinea?

00:04:46.921 --> 00:04:48.381
And I've just completed
a year in the fields.

00:04:48.548 --> 00:04:50.633
I'm writing a book
about magical creatures.

00:04:51.134 --> 00:04:52.761
Like an extermination guide?

00:04:53.386 --> 00:04:55.221
No, a guide to help people understand

00:04:55.388 --> 00:04:57.599
why we should be protecting
these creatures instead of killing them.

00:04:57.766 --> 00:04:58.892
MR. ABERNATHY: Goldstein?

00:04:59.434 --> 00:05:00.477
Where is she?

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:03.021
Where is she? Goldstein?

00:05:04.439 --> 00:05:05.440
Goldstein?

00:05:07.233 --> 00:05:09.694
Did you just butt in
on the investigative team again?

00:05:14.824 --> 00:05:15.825
Where have you been?

00:05:16.159 --> 00:05:17.202
What?

00:05:18.036 --> 00:05:19.621
Where'd she pick you up?

00:05:20.747 --> 00:05:21.831
Me?

00:05:23.333 --> 00:05:25.668
Have you been tracking
them Second Salemers again?

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:27.420
Of course not, sir.

00:05:30.173 --> 00:05:32.050
Afternoon, Mr. Graves, sir.

00:05:32.217 --> 00:05:34.135
Afternoon, Abernathy.

00:05:34.844 --> 00:05:37.180
Mr. Graves, sir, this is Mr. Scamander.

00:05:37.347 --> 00:05:38.932
He has a crazy creature in that case,

00:05:39.098 --> 00:05:41.643
and it got out
and caused mayhem in a bank.

00:05:43.019 --> 00:05:44.521
Let's see the little guy.

00:05:47.732 --> 00:05:48.733
(STAMMERS)

00:05:58.535 --> 00:05:59.536
(LOCK CLICKS OPEN)

00:06:08.211 --> 00:06:09.212
(SNIFFING)

00:06:12.465 --> 00:06:13.550
Tina.

00:06:14.676 --> 00:06:16.386
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

00:06:29.774 --> 00:06:30.775
(RUSTLES)

00:06:34.445 --> 00:06:35.864
I'm sorry, Grandma.

